    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Saying what you do for a living",
     "texto": [
      "Hva jobber du med? is used to ask «What do you do for a living?». Although literally it means «What do you work with?», it is not translated word for word.",
      "To say «I work as», use jobber som: Jeg jobber som lærer. With er or jobber som, the job name usually has no article, unlike English «I am a teacher»: Jeg er lærer, not «jeg er en lærer» in this basic introduction.",
      "Studerer means «I study». Like the other present-tense verbs, it keeps the same form for jeg and du."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
